From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:39:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: don't require DAPF ranges on a
 DART that has none

T8132's ISP DART names a dapf register page without apple,dapf-ranges, and
its probe failed since the sleep series began parsing the ranges.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 36e50de19710c23f0d8af1a4ee815d59d92e9307)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index fb2a962842..cc27296ba2 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -5101,7 +5101,9 @@ static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			return PTR_ERR(dart->gapf);
 		dart->gapf_boot = readl(dart->gapf);
 	}
-	if (platform_get_resource_byname(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, "dapf")) {
+	/* T8132's ISP DART names its DAPF page but has no ranges to restore. */
+	if (platform_get_resource_byname(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, "dapf") &&
+	    of_property_present(pdev->dev.of_node, "apple,dapf-ranges")) {
 		ret = apple_dart_dapf_parse(pdev, dart);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
-- 
